<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 30 May, from 1431 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1431">1431 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">595 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is burned at the stake in Rouen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Condemned as a relapsed heretic by a church court under English control, Joan died aged about 19. Her conviction was annulled in 1456, and she was canonised in 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1498">1498 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">528 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sails on his third voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> left Sanlúcar de Barrameda with six ships. He reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and the Paria peninsula of Venezuela, his first sight of the South American mainland.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1593">1593 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">433 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Marlowe is killed in Deptford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The playwright of Doctor Faustus was stabbed by Ingram Frizer during a dispute over a bill. His links to government espionage have fuelled theories about his death ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">America's first daily newspaper appears in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benjamin Towne's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> Evening Post began publishing daily, the first newspaper in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to do so. It folded the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Biafra declares independence from Nigeria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel Odumegwu Ojukwu proclaimed the Republic of Biafra in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s south-east. The civil war that followed lasted until 1970, and up to two million people died, many from famine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Students unveil the Goddess of Democracy in Tiananmen Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Art students erected a ten-metre statue facing Mao's portrait as a symbol of the pro-democracy movement. Troops destroyed it when they cleared the square on 4 June.</p></div></li></ol>
